ring>'`` for string input\n   when no source name is supplied), ``lineno`` (the one-based line\n   number of the offending continuation line), and ``line`` (the raw\n   text of the offending line, which may lack a final newline).\n   All three values are stored as attributes of the same name and\n   are preserved in ``args`` for pickling and copying.\n\n   .. attribute:: source\n\n   .. attribute:: lineno\n\n   .. attribute:: line","old":".. exception:: MultilineContinuationError\n\n   Raised when an indented continuation line follows a valueless option\n   (an option with no value, as permitted by ``allow_no_value=True``).\n   This is a subclass of :exc:`!ParsingError`.\n\n   The constructor takes three arguments: ``source`` (the name of the\n   source being parsed, or ``'<string>'`` for string input), ``lineno``\n   (the one-based line number of the offending continuation line), and\n   ``line`` (the exact text of that line, including its trailing\n   newline).  All three values are stored as attributes of the same\n   name and are preserved in ``args`` for pickling and copying.\n\n   .. attribute:: source\n\n   .. attribute:: lineno\n\n   .. attribute:: line\n\n   .. versionadded:: 3.12","path":"Doc/library/configparser.rst"},"id":"C18","index":2,"observation":null,"origin":"model","passed":null,"sequence":60},{"accepted":true,"action":{"action":"record_account","text":"Task complete: all three reviewer findings addressed in Doc/library/configparser.rst. Documentation verified accurate against implementation (relative indentation check, blank/comment handling, source default, line may lack newline, no versionadded). Running public check on candidate 6c031ad9."},"id":"C19","index":1,"observation":null,"origin":"model_authored_account","passed":null,"sequence":61},{"accepted":true,"action":{"action":"check","check_id":"public","expected_candidate_id":"6c031ad9a4622eed24e4bba58b2c5ef6f670aae9a163e58832355808e496c6ef"},"id":"C19","index":2,"observation":"CHK-0062","o